If you attempt to convert an altar and fail, you lose
luck.  Since the chance of successful conversion is
based on XP and the chance is poor lower than XP=3D5
early altars aren't useful for sac fests  ...  yet.

> Corpses
> rot after 50 turns, which means you have to kill them near the
> altar...and often if you find a coaligned altar on level 1 or 3 or so
> forth, there aren't that many monsters around.

Also noting the sac fest doesn't start until it's a co-aligned
altar.

> Is a wand/scroll/book of create monster a necessary requirement for a
> "sac fest"?

Not necessary.  It works best if you have hungerless
cast of create monster, but the principles apply no matter
how many monsters you sacrafice.  Only one large monster
on a level, bait it to follow you to the altar and there's some
benefit to offering it.

Sac fest discussions tend to be about large numbers of
offerings so they get the benefit of statistics.  Low numbers
still have statistics, but they get a different view of them
because of the randomness.

If you want an artifact it's worth it.  If you want luck it's
worth it.  And so on.  Use up what monsters do appear,
then move on.


